# Global leaderboard config. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in.
# The backend is the Cloudflare Worker in `worker/` — see worker/README.md for
# how to deploy it and where this URL comes from.
#
# When VITE_LEADERBOARD_API is absent the global leaderboard disables gracefully
# and the game runs fully offline (local Hall of High Scores only).

# Base URL of the deployed Worker, no trailing slash.
# e.g. https://order-of-order-leaderboard.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev
VITE_LEADERBOARD_API=
# Optional. Must match the Worker's SUBMIT_KEY secret when you set one. This
# ships in the client bundle, so it is a bot filter, not a secret — leave both
# sides blank to run without it.
VITE_LEADERBOARD_SUBMIT_KEY=

# Build flags (see src/buildFlags.ts) are normally set per build rather than
# here — target-specific ones come from committed mode env files such as
# `.env.itch` and `.env.phone`.
# Uncomment to preview the gold frame from a plain `npm run dev` / `npm run build`.
# VITE_GOLD_BORDER=true
